        <definition>SDK_CAPI CUVIS_STATUS SDK_CCALL cuvis_calib_create_from_path</definition>
        <argsstring>(const CUVIS_CHAR *i_factoryDir, CUVIS_CALIB *o_pCalibration)</argsstring>
        <name>cuvis_calib_create_from_path</name>
        <param>
          <type>const <ref refid="cuvis_8h_1ad6fd13ac609b8cbfad5f49e5ff0e11d3" kindref="member">CUVIS_CHAR</ref> *</type>
          <declname>i_factoryDir</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="cuvis_8h_1a00367af6d90a7820cfb054901dee4061" kindref="member">CUVIS_CALIB</ref> *</type>
          <declname>o_pCalibration</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Create a calibration from factory path. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The calibration is created from a factory path, containing the license and calibration file &quot;init.daq&quot; as well as further calibration files (e.g. SpRad.cu3).</para>
<para>The calibration is lazy-loading, i.e. the AcquisitionContext and the ProcessingContext will only be initialized, when explicitly called.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>do not load multiple calibration instances of the same camera</para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">i_factoryDir</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The path to the factory directory </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">o_pCalibration</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>the handle of the calibration </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><ref refid="group__cuvis__returns_1ggaa06c62ba25240f4763da0e590ebf3b9dad52787b0cfb0da2c053a68bcdc54bc6f" kindref="member">status_ok</ref> if the calibration could be loaded </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
