    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Functions to interact with a calibration object of the SDK.</para>
<para>There are two ways to create a calibration object. One way is by loading it specifically from a factory directory (see <ref refid="group__cuvis__calib_1ga5dab63eb810fa988d1fbe68ce982d9f0" kindref="member">cuvis_calib_create_from_path</ref>). The other one is by loading it from a session file. The Calibration object is needed to load other parts of the SDK like the <ref refid="group__cuvis__acq" kindref="compound">Acquisition Context</ref> and the <ref refid="group__cuvis__proc" kindref="compound">Processing Context</ref>. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
